{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport secrets,json\nnames=['Astro Brouhaha','Astro Rumble','Astro Scramble','Astro Kerfuffle','Astro Tussle','Cosmic Coverfire','Astro Brickade','Astro Hullabaloo','Astro Battlebeans','Space Invaderade','Astro Skirmish','Astro Bonk Brigade','Star Barricade','Astro Block Party','Astro Salvo','Astro Ruckus','Battle of the Astro Bastions','Space Rebuilders','Astro Afterparty','Astro Blastoff','Astro Rattle','Star Invade-aid','Astro Blast Brigade','Cosmic Brick Brawl','Astro Shelter Skelter','Astro Counterpunch','Astro Patch Patrol','Astro Panic Picnic','Astro Battle Buddies','Astro Battleworks','Astro Star Spat','Space Invader Insurance','Astro Battle Bloom','Astro Scrap Stars','Astro Battle Bop','Astro Bunker Bonanza','Astro Battle Pals','Astro Moon Melee','Astro Battlement','Astro Star Scuffle','Astro Invader Evader','Astro Brick Blitz','Astro Battle Stationery','Space Invaders Anonymous','Astro Battle Rally','Astro Battle Sprouts','Astro Cover Club','Astro Planet Patrol','Astro Siege Sneeze','Astro Battle Jam']\nassert len(names)==50\ntitle=names[secrets.randbelow(len(names))]\nslug=title.replace(' ','-')+'-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022645'\nPath(slug).mkdir()\nPath('workspace.json').write_text(json.dumps({'title':title,'folder':slug,'html':slug+'.html'},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPath('PROGRESS.md').write_text('# Build progress\\\\n\\\\n## Task and deliverables\\\\n- Build PLAN.md using TASK.md, keeping all development files in \"'`'\"'+slug+'/\"'`.'\"\\\\n- Title selected with a real random-number generator from 50 original candidates: **'+title+'**.\\\\n- Root deliverables: \"'`'\"'+slug+'.html\"'`, `exit-interview.json`, this progress log.'\"\\\\n- Apply home AGENTS instructions and game-toolchain skill. No subagents requested.\\\\n\\\\n## Current phase\\\\nReading and pinning engine/Hub contracts; examining source evidence. No implementation yet.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance checklist\\\\n- [ ] Pinned native engine and pristine Hub client; isolated single-file boot.\\\\n- [ ] Deterministic fixed-step combat, swept hits, cell bunkers/repair, deployments/scores.\\\\n- [ ] Solo and simultaneous local co-op; host/guest/server Hub authority.\\\\n- [ ] Six authored formations, three locations, two-phase flagship, ordinary-rules campaign tests.\\\\n- [ ] Controller/mouse/keyboard/touch UI, settings, records, paged credits/feedback.\\\\n- [ ] Attract loop and pause developer tools; assisted record separation.\\\\n- [ ] Quiet verification command, browser/audio/Hub tests, visual inspection, issue log.\\\\n- [ ] Final export, exact interview schema, truthful final report.\\\\n\\\\n## Environment and constraints\\\\nUse installed Python Playwright at \"'`/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python`. No browser installation. Servers only 127.0.0.1 port 0, retain PID and stop only owned process. No files in /tmp or sibling run folders.'\"\\\\n')\nfor sub in ['vendor/engine','vendor/hub','src','tools','tests','evidence']:\n (Path(slug)/sub).mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nprint(json.dumps({'title':title,'folder':slug}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
