{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat vendor/engine/README.md vendor/hub/README.md'","aggregated_output":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.89.1)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\nis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\nare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\nlacks.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n7. **A game in real 3D** (first person, a light gun, a racer on banked roads, flight, a dungeon crawled in 3D, fixed\n   cameras): the 2D views have no perspective camera, but the engine has a 3D add-on, `World3D` (three.js r182 and\n   Rapier 0.19.3 under the 2D engine, which keeps the HUD, menus and sound). It is not in this folder: take\n   `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js` (its header is its manual), `vendor/` and the 3D kit closest to your game\n   (`src/starter3d/`) from the repository, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge, and see them play at\n   my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page, writing every `</script` inside them as `<\\/script` (the agent edition's header has one,\nand the page would end there).\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped unless\nthe game is made with `draw: true` (the template is): then each `advance` draws a frame on a stand-in, and a draw error\nlands in `game.errors`, as it would on a player's screen.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n- `game.go('play')` fades for `game.fadeTime` (.22 s) before the new scene enters: advance past it, or set\n  `game.fadeTime = 0` in a test.\n- A scene change clears `game.after` and `game.every` timers (`{ keep: true }` outlives it); those made before the first\n  scene live into it. It ends a hit-stop; `game.timeScale` stays (restore a slow motion with a kept timer). A boot step's `game.go(name)` enters that scene when the boot ends.\n- Draw changes nothing, and nothing your update or input relies on (a click target, what is on screen) may be made only\n  in `draw`: `E.Menu`'s rows come from its update (`menu.rowAt(i)` is entry i's box, for a test's click), and the camera\n  (`game.cam`) says where the screen is in update.\n- `E.store` keeps values for the visit in Node, which has no `localStorage` (`E.store.clear()` between games in one test).\n- A script's `tap` and `hold` are no device: `input.label()` keeps showing the keys or buttons the player used last.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card, longer if one asks for more time: what\n   the game is, how to win, the controls. The card is the hub's, from the\n   game's tags, or the game's own (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. A player can ask for more time, which adds\nten seconds; while more than half of them are asking, the countdown holds.\nBy default the hub shows its own card over the game. A game can make the\ncard its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat vendor/engine/kits/arcade.js vendor/engine/game/test.mjs'","aggregated_output":"// The ARCADE kit's game (a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/32-arcade.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. arcade.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs arcade runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 10  ARCADE  (a cabinet of three golden-age classics: Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids). @modules arcade grid gen\n * Three short games, each a remaster (lit, with HD rigs, glowing lines and particles) with the classic look one key away\n * (C, a pad's Y, or Settings: Arcade, Look), each with its own high-score table, initials on a letter wheel, a continue,\n * two players taking turns, and a demo in the attract mode.\n *   MAZE (#arcade/maze): eat every glow-seed in a hedge maze while four wisps hunt you, each its own way (one chases, one\n *     heads you off, one flanks with the first, one is shy up close), in waves of scatter and chase; a lantern seed turns\n *     them blue and edible for a while; the side tunnel wraps round. Each maze is new (E.gen's braided maze, mirrored);\n *     an intermission after the first.\n *   FORMATION (#arcade/formation): moths fly in on curved paths (E.Path), form up and sway, then dive at you along paths\n *     of their own, turning as they fly (r.sprite's rot); two shots on screen at a time; a stage card between waves.\n *   ROCKS (#arcade/rocks): turn, thrust and drift through a field of rocks that split when shot; the screen's edges meet\n *     (E.wrap); a saucer hunts you; hyperspace when cornered. Glowing vector lines.\n * The cabinet (#arcade) is the title: left and right pick a game, up and down one or two players. Left alone it plays a\n * demo of each game in turn (its own bot), then shows that game's table. The sides of a wide screen show cabinet art\n * drawn by code. Keys: arrows / WASD, Space / Z / J fire (rocks: up thrusts, X / K hyperspace), Enter start, C classic.\n * TOUCH: the stick, FIRE (rocks: THRUST and WARP too); a tap picks a cabinet, and the letter wheel takes taps.\n * HOW IT WORKS: E.Arcade (the arcade module) keeps the scores, lives, turns, tables, initials, cards, the continue and the\n * attract mode; the maze is an E.Grid with E.GridMovers (a turn asked early is kept), each game a { begin, step, draw }.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst ARCADE = (() => {\n  const KEYS = Object.assign({}, E.Input.SHMUP, { thrust: ['Pad2', 'Pad5'], warp: ['KeyX', 'KeyK', 'ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1', 'Pad6'], classic: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'] });\n  delete KEYS.bomb;\n  game.settings.define({ key: 'arcadeLook', group: 'Arcade', label: 'Look', options: [['remaster', 'Remaster'], ['classic', 'Classic']], value: 'remaster', help: 'Remaster: lit, with HD rigs and glowing lines. Classic: as the cabinets first looked. C switches it in play' });\n  const classic = () => game.settings.arcadeLook === 'classic';\n  // the cabinet's own tune (the step sequencer's format): A minor, a bouncing bass\n  const SONG = { bpm: 132, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .12, notes: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 - G5 . E5 . C5 . D5 . | E5 - - . D5 . C5 . B4 . G4 . A4 - - . | F4 . A4 . C5 . F5 - E5 . C5 . A4 . B4 . | C5 . B4 . A4 . G#4 . A4 - - - - . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . | C3 . C4 . C3 . C4 . G2 . G3 . G2 . G3 . | F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . | E2 . E3 . E2 . E3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .12, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h' }] };\n  // the remaster's deep space (the classic look keeps plain black): a planet, nebulae drifting, many stars\n  const SPACE = [['#020208', '#0a0a24', '#1a0c30', '#2a1038'], ['#02040a', '#06142a', '#0c1c3a', '#1a1a3a']].map((sky, i) => new E.Backdrop({ sky, moon: { x: i ? .16 : .82, y: i ? .7 : .22, r: i ? 22 : 15, color: i ? '#8ab0d8' : '#b89ae8' }, stars: 140,\n    layers: [{ kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#1a4a6a' : '#6a3aa8', y: .3, height: .45, parallax: .03, drift: 1, nebula: true, seed: 2 + i }, { kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#3a2a5a' : '#2a5ab0', y: .72, height: .4, parallax: .05, drift: 2, nebula: true, seed: 5 + i }] }));\n  // cabinet art round a playfield of one fixed screen: on a wide screen's sides (left of x0, right of x1) a lit bezel edge,\n  // a marquee stripe and drifting sparks; on a tall one (above y0, below y1) the marquee with the game's name and the\n  // control panel\n  function cabinet(r, x0, x1, hue, y0 = 0, y1 = r.H, label = '') {\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      const H = r.H, t = game.time;\n      if (y0 > 40) {\n        px.rect(g, 0, 0, r.W, y0 - 4, '#0a0614'); px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 34, hue[0]); px.blend(g, .25, 'add', () => px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 12, '#ffffff'));\n        E.font.title(g, label, r.W / 2, y0 - 42, { align: 'center', scale: 2, colors: ['#ffffff', '#1a1030'], depth: 1 });\n      }\n      if (H - y1 > 40) {\n        const y = y1 + 6; px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, H - y, '#140c22'); px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, 2, hue[0]);\n        const cy = y + Math.min(40, (H - y) / 2); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy, 8, '#2a1a3e'); px.rect(g, r.W / 2 - 51, cy - 16, 3, 16, '#c8c8d0'); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy - 17, 5, '#ff4a4a');\n        for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.disc(g, r.W / 2 + 10 + i * 18, cy, 6, hue[i]);\n      }\n      for (const [a, b, right] of [[0, x0, false], [x1, r.W, true]]) {\n        if (b - a < 3) continue;\n        // the side's art: a dark panel tinted toward the game's colour, lit stripes slanting across it\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) px.rect(g, a, Math.floor(H * i / 8), b - a, Math.ceil(H / 8) + 1, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .03 + i * .018));\n        g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(a, 0, b - a, H); g.clip();\n        for (let x = a - H; x < b + 40; x += 46) { const k = right ? 1 : -1, x1 = right ? x : b - (x - a); px.blend(g, .1, 'add', () => px.poly(g, [[x1, 0], [x1 + 18 * k, 0], [x1 + 18 * k + H * .5 * k, H], [x1 + H * .5 * k, H]], hue[1])); }\n        const sw = (y0, y1, c) => px.poly(g, right ? [[a, H * y0], [b, H * (y0 - .3)], [b, H * (y1 - .3)], [a, H * y1]] : [[b, H * y0], [a, H * (y0 - .3)], [a, H * (y1 - .3)], [b, H * y1]], c);\n        sw(.5, .74, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .7)); sw(.5, .52, '#ffffff'); sw(.76, .8, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[1], .8));   // a swoosh in the game's colours\n        g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n        if (label && b - a >= 44) { const n = label.length, k = Math.min(4, Math.floor((H - 20) / n / 9)), y0 = Math.round(H / 2 - n * k * 4.5); for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) E.font.title(g, label[i], (a + b) / 2, y0 + i * k * 9, { align: 'center', scale: k, colors: ['#ffffff', E.shade(hue[0], .3), hue[0]], depth: 2 }); }   // the game's name down the side\n        for (let y = -24; y < H; y += 24) { const yy = Math.round(y + (t * 20) % 24); px.rect(g, right ? a + 6 : b - 10, yy, 4, 12, hue[1]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 14 : b - 18, yy + 12, 2, 6, hue[2]); }\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) { const y = (i * 61 + t * (12 + i * 3)) % (H + 20) - 10, x = right ? a + 10 + (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14) : b - 10 - (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14); px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x, y, 1 + i % 3, hue[i % 3])); }\n        px.rect(g, right ? a : b - 3, 0, 3, H, hue[0]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 3 : b - 4, 0, 1, H, '#ffffff');\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  /* =================================== 1. MAZE =================================== */\n  const MAZE = (() => {\n    const C8 = 8, MW = 29, MH = 31, TUN = 17, HX = 10, HY = 11, DOOR = [14, 10], WCOL = ['#ff4a4a', '#ff9ad8', '#4ae8ff', '#ffb84a'];\n    const CORNER = [[MW - 2, -3], [1, -3], [MW - 1, MH], [0, MH]], PHASES = [7, 20, 7, 20, 5, 20, 5, 1e9], WAYS = [[0, -1], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0]];   // (up, left, down, right: the original's order for ties)\n    let cells, grid, wgrid, start, seeds, power, hero = null, wisps = null, mode, modeT, phase, fright, eaten, level, cab, demo, over, deathT, readyT, inter, berry, ate, X0 = 0, Y0 = 12;\n    const key = (x, y) => x + ',' + y, cellOf = k => k.split(',').map(Number);\n    const nearest = (x, y, ok) => { let best = [x, y], bd = 1e9; for (let b = 0; b < MH; b++) for (let a = 0; a < MW; a++) if (ok(a, b)) { const d = Math.abs(a - x) + Math.abs(b - y); if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = [a, b]; } } return best; };\n    const ring = (x, y) => y >= HY - 1 && y <= HY + 5 && x >= HX - 1 && x <= HX + 9;\n    // a new maze: the left half from E.gen's braided maze, mirrored; doors in the middle wall; the wisps' house in a ring\n    // of hall; the tunnel's ends opened. The same level gives the same maze\n    function build() {\n      const half = E.gen.maze(15, MH, { seed: 7 + level * 13, braid: 1 }).rows;\n      cells = half.map(r => (r + r.slice(0, 14).split('').reverse().join('')).split(''));\n      for (let y = 1; y < MH - 1; y += 4) if (cells[y][13] === '.') cells[y][14] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY - 1; y <= HY + 5; y++) for (let x = HX - 1; x <= HX + 9; x++) cells[y][x] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY; y <= HY + 4; y++) for (let x = HX; x <= HX + 8; x++) cells[y][x] = y === HY || y === HY + 4 || x === HX || x === HX + 8 ? '#' : 'H';\n      cells[HY][14] = '-'; cells[TUN][0] = cells[TUN][MW - 1] = '.';\n      grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' });       // yours\n      wgrid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] !== '#' });      // the wisps' (the house too: openFor says when)\n      start = nearest(14, 23, (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y));\n      seeds = new Set(); power = new Set(); ate = 0; berry = null;\n      for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 1; x < MW - 1; x++) if (cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y) && !(x === start[0] && y === start[1])) seeds.add(key(x, y));\n      for (const [x, y] of [[1, 3], [MW - 2, 3], [1, MH - 4], [MW - 2, MH - 4]]) { const k = key(...nearest(x, y, (a, b) => seeds.has(key(a, b)))); seeds.delete(k); power.add(k); }\n    }\n    // everyone to their places: you below the house, the first wisp at its door, the others inside waiting their turn\n    function reset() {\n      hero = { m: new E.GridMover({ cx: start[0], cy: start[1], speed: 7.5 }), dir: [-1, 0], chomp: 0, dying: 0 };\n      hero.m.dir = [-1, 0];\n      const was = wisps;\n      wisps = WCOL.map((c, i) => ({ i, c, m: new E.GridMover({ cx: i ? 10 + i * 2 : DOOR[0], cy: i ? HY + 2 : DOOR[1], speed: 6.8 }), home: i > 0, wait: i * 2.5, eyes: false, leaving: false, blue: false,\n        rig: was ? was[i].rig : new E.Blob({ R: 3.6, face: 'front', colors: { dk: E.shade(c, -.35), base: c, lt: E.shade(c, .35) } }) }));\n      for (const w of wisps) w.m.dir = [w.i % 2 ? 1 : -1, 0];\n      mode = 'scatter'; modeT = 0; phase = 0; fright = 0; eaten = 0; readyT = 1.8; deathT = 0;\n    }\n    // where each aims while chasing: at you; four cells ahead of you; past a point two ahead, as far again as the first wisp\n    // is behind it (they pincer); at you from afar, its corner up close. Scattering: its corner. Eyes and leavers: the door\n    function target(w) {\n      if (w.eyes || w.leaving) return DOOR;\n      if (mode === 'scatter') return CORNER[w.i];\n      const h = hero.m, [dx, dy] = hero.dir;\n      if (w.i === 0) return [h.cx, h.cy];\n      if (w.i === 1) return [h.cx + dx * 4, h.cy + dy * 4];\n      if (w.i === 2) { const a = wisps[0].m; return [(h.cx + dx * 2) * 2 - a.cx, (h.cy + dy * 2) * 2 - a.cy]; }\n      return Math.hypot(w.m.cx - h.cx, w.m.cy - h.cy) > 8 ? [h.cx, h.cy] : CORNER[3];\n    }\n    const openFor = (w, x, y) => { if (x < 0 || x >= MW) return y === TUN; const c = cells[y] && cells[y][x]; return c === '.' || ((c === 'H' || c === '-') && (w.eyes || w.leaving)); };\n    // at each cell a wisp takes the open way (never straight back) nearest its target; blue, a random one; eyes, the\n    // grid's path home\n    function choose(w) {\n      const m = w.m;\n      if (w.eyes) { const p = grid.path([m.cx, m.cy], DOOR); if (p.length > 1) return [p[1][0] - m.cx, p[1][1] - m.cy]; }\n      const ways = WAYS.filter(([a, b]) => !(a === -m.dir[0] && b === -m.dir[1]) && openFor(w, m.cx + a, m.cy + b));\n      if (!ways.length) return [-m.dir[0], -m.dir[1]];\n      if (w.blue) return ways[Math.floor(Math.random() * ways.length)];\n      const t = target(w), d = c => (m.cx + c[0] - t[0]) ** 2 + (m.cy + c[1] - t[1]) ** 2;\n      return ways.reduce((p, q) => d(q) < d(p) ? q : p);\n    }\n    // the tunnel: off one end, on at the other, going the same way\n    function wrapTunnel(m) { if (m.cy !== TUN || m.moving) return; if (m.cx === 0 && m.dir[0] < 0) { m.place(MW - 1, TUN); m.dir = [-1, 0]; } else if (m.cx === MW - 1 && m.dir[0] > 0) { m.place(0, TUN); m.dir = [1, 0]; } }\n    const dirOf = v => Math.hypot(v[0], v[1]) < .4 ? null : Math.abs(v[0]) > Math.abs(v[1]) ? [Math.sign(v[0]), 0] : [0, Math.sign(v[1])];\n    const pos = m => ({ x: X0 + (m.x + .5) * C8, y: Y0 + (m.y + .5) * C8 });\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      if (inter) return;   // (the intermission is a script: it moves its own actors)\n      if (readyT > 0) { readyT -= dt; return; }\n      const h = hero.m;\n      if (deathT > 0) { hero.dying = deathT; if ((deathT -= dt) <= 0) lost(); return; }\n      if (fright > 0) { if ((fright -= dt) <= 0) for (const w of wisps) w.blue = false; }\n      else if ((modeT += dt) > PHASES[phase]) { modeT = 0; phase = Math.min(PHASES.length - 1, phase + 1); mode = phase % 2 ? 'chase' : 'scatter'; }\n      // you: the stick's way, kept until it can be taken (a turn asked early), going on until a wall\n      h.update(dt, grid, demo ? botDir() : dirOf(I.move()), { keep: true });\n      if (h.moving) hero.dir = h.dir;\n      wrapTunnel(h); hero.chomp = Math.max(0, hero.chomp - dt);\n      const k = key(h.cx, h.cy);\n      if (seeds.delete(k)) { cab.add(10); ate++; hero.chomp = .25; A.sfx('blip', { vol: .25, pitch: ate % 2 ? 1 : 1.2 }); if (ate === 70 || ate === 170) berry = { t: 9 }; }\n      if (power.delete(k)) { cab.add(50); fright = Math.max(1.5, 7 - level); eaten = 0; for (const w of wisps) w.blue = !w.eyes; A.sfx('powerup'); P.ring(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 2, 30, '#ffd060', .4); }\n      if (berry && (berry.t -= dt) <= 0) berry = null;\n      if (berry && h.cx === 14 && h.cy === TUN) { cab.add(100 * level, pos(h)); berry = null; A.sfx('pickup'); P.glints(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 4, 6, '#ff8a8a'); }\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const m = w.m;\n        if (w.home) { if ((w.wait -= dt) > 0) { m.y = HY + 2 + Math.sin(game.time * 6 + w.i) * .3; continue; } w.home = false; w.leaving = true; m.y = m.cy; }\n        m.speed = w.eyes ? 15 : w.blue ? 4.2 : m.cy === TUN && (m.cx < 5 || m.cx > MW - 6) ? 4 : 6.6 + level * .25;\n        m.update(dt, wgrid, m.moving ? null : choose(w), { blocked: (x, y) => !openFor(w, x, y) });\n        wrapTunnel(m);\n        if (!m.moving && m.cx === DOOR[0] && m.cy === DOOR[1]) { w.leaving = false; if (w.eyes) { w.eyes = false; w.blue = false; } }\n        if (!w.eyes && Math.abs(m.x - h.x) + Math.abs(m.y - h.y) < .8) {\n          if (w.blue) { w.eyes = true; w.blue = false; eaten++; cab.add(200 * 2 ** (eaten - 1), pos(m)); A.sfx('kick'); game.freeze(.3); P.sparks(pos(m).x, pos(m).y, 2, 8); }\n          else { deathT = 1.5; A.sfx('die'); return; }\n        }\n      }\n      if (!seeds.size && !power.size) { level++; cab.card('MAZE ' + level, 2); A.sfx('oneup'); if (level === 2 && !demo) intermission(); build(); reset(); readyT = 2.2; }\n    }\n    // after the death's turn: a life gone; the other player's maze (two players, each keeps theirs), or the end\n    function lost() {\n      const was = cab.p, r = cab.die();\n      if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; }\n      if (r === 'next') { was.save = { level, seeds, power, ate }; const s = cab.p.save; level = s ? s.level : 1; build(); if (s) ({ seeds, power, ate } = s); }\n      reset();\n    }\n    // the intermission (a script): a wisp chases you across, then you come back big and chase it\n    function intermission() {\n      const a = { x: -30, big: false }; inter = a;\n      game.script(function* () { yield game.tween(a, { x: MW * C8 + 40 }, 2.6, { ease: 'linear' }); a.big = true; yield .4; yield game.tween(a, { x: -60 }, 2.2, { ease: 'linear' }); yield .3; inter = null; });\n    }\n    // the demo's player (the attract mode, and tools/kits-test.mjs): it counts the steps to every cell, its own and the\n    // wisps' (breadth first, through the tunnel); a cell is safe when it gets there two steps before any of them. It goes\n    // the safe way to the nearest seed (a lantern when they close in, a blue wisp while there is time), else to the\n    // neighbour they reach last\n    function steps(from, ok) {\n      const D = new Map(), up = new Map(); let q = [];\n      for (const [c, d] of from) { const k = key(...c); if (!D.has(k) || D.get(k) > d) { D.set(k, d); q.push(c); } }\n      while (q.length) {\n        const n = [];\n        for (const c of q) { const d = D.get(key(...c)); for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = c[0] + a; const y = c[1] + b; if (y === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; const k = key(x, y); if (!grid.walk([x, y]) || D.has(k) || (ok && !ok(x, y, d + 1))) continue; D.set(k, d + 1); up.set(k, c); n.push([x, y]); } }\n        q = n;\n      }\n      return { D, up };\n    }\n    function botDir() {\n      const h = hero.m; if (h.moving) return null;\n      const src = [];\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        if (w.eyes || w.blue) continue;\n        if (w.home || w.leaving) { if (!w.home || w.wait < 2) src.push([DOOR, w.home ? 3 : 1]); continue; }\n        src.push([[w.m.cx, w.m.cy], 0]); const n = [w.m.cx + w.m.dir[0], w.m.cy + w.m.dir[1]]; if (grid.walk(n)) src.push([n, 0]);\n      }\n      const W = steps(src).D, wd = (x, y) => W.has(key(x, y)) ? W.get(key(x, y)) : 99, safe = (x, y, d) => d + 2 < wd(x, y);\n      const S = steps([[[h.cx, h.cy], 0]], safe), near = wd(h.cx, h.cy) < 7;\n      const goals = fright > 2.5 && wisps.some(w => w.blue) ? wisps.filter(w => w.blue).map(w => key(w.m.cx, w.m.cy)) : near && [...power].some(k => S.D.has(k)) ? [...power] : [...seeds, ...power];\n      let best = null, bd = 1e9; for (const k of goals) { const d = S.D.get(k); if (d > 0 && d < bd) { bd = d; best = k; } }\n      if (best) { let c = cellOf(best), p; while ((p = S.up.get(key(...c))) && !(p[0] === h.cx && p[1] === h.cy)) c = p; return [Math.sign(E.wrapDiff(h.cx, c[0], MW)), c[1] - h.cy]; }\n      let far = null, fd = -1;\n      for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = h.cx + a; if (h.cy === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; if (grid.walk([x, h.cy + b]) && wd(x, h.cy + b) > fd) { fd = wd(x, h.cy + b); far = [a, b]; } }\n      return far;\n    }\n    function layout() { X0 = Math.round((game.W - MW * C8) / 2); Y0 = Math.max(12, Math.round((game.H - MH * C8) / 2)); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), t = game.time, [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), bx = ox + X0, by = oy + Y0;\n      r.sky(cl ? ['#000000', '#000000'] : ['#04030c', '#0a0820', '#120a28']);\n      // the maze on the floor (lit in the remaster: hedges with a sunlit top edge and a shadow at the foot; the classic's\n      // thin blue lines facing the halls)\n      r.decal(g => {\n        const wall = (x, y) => !!cells[y] && cells[y][x] === '#';\n        for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n          const c = cells[y][x], X = bx + x * C8, Y = by + y * C8;\n          if (c === '#') {\n            if (cl) { px.col(g, '#2121de'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + 2, C8, 1); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + C8 - 3, C8, 1); if (!wall(x - 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + 2, Y, 1, C8); if (!wall(x + 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + C8 - 3, Y, 1, C8); }\n            else { px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, '#1c4a22'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, 2, '#5aa84a'); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y + C8 - 2, C8, 2, '#0c2410'); if (E.hash2(x, y) < .3) px.dot(g, X + 2 + (x * 3) % 4, Y + 3 + (y * 5) % 3, '#7ac860'); }\n          } else if (c === '-') px.rect(g, X, Y + 3, C8, 2, cl ? '#ffb8ff' : '#e0a0ff');\n          else if (!cl) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, (x + y) % 2 ? '#141026' : '#171230');\n        }\n      });\n      // the seeds, lanterns and the berry: glowing (they stay bright under the light)\n      r.queue(0, -1e4, 0, g => {\n        for (const k of seeds) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 3, Y = by + y * C8 + 3; px.rect(g, X, Y, 2, 2, cl ? '#ffb897' : '#ffe9a0'); if (!cl) px.dot(g, X, Y, '#ffffff'); }\n        if (Math.floor(t * 4) % 2 || readyT > 0) for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 4, Y = by + y * C8 + 4; if (cl) px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#ffb897'); else { px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, X, Y, 6, '#ffb030')); px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#fff4c0'); } }\n        if (berry) { const X = bx + 14 * C8 + 4, Y = by + TUN * C8 + 4; px.disc(g, X - 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.disc(g, X + 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.dot(g, X - 2, Y, '#ffb0b0'); px.rect(g, X - 1, Y - 3, 3, 1, '#4ad84a'); }\n      }, { emissive: true, bias: -1e6 });\n      if (!cl) { L.add(pos(hero.m).x, pos(hero.m).y, 8, 60, 1.2, { color: '#ffe890' }); for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k); L.add(X0 + x * C8 + 4, Y0 + y * C8 + 4, 6, 26, .7, { color: '#ffb040' }); } }\n      if (inter) { drawInter(r); return; }\n      // you: a lit sphere with a chomping mouth (classic: the flat yellow disc); dying, the mouth opens until you are gone\n      const hp = pos(hero.m), ang = Math.atan2(hero.dir[1], hero.dir[0]), open = hero.dying > 0 ? Math.PI * (1 - hero.dying / 1.5) : (hero.m.moving || hero.chomp > 0 ? Math.abs(Math.sin(t * 16)) : .3) * .9;\n      if (hero.dying <= 0 || open < Math.PI * .98) r.actor(hp.x, hp.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n        y -= 0; const R = 4;\n        if (cl) px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#ffe000'); else { px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#d8a010'); px.disc(g, x - .5, y - .5, R - 1, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 1.5, y - 1.5, 1.5, '#fff8c0'); }\n        if (open > .05) px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x + Math.cos(ang - open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang - open) * 7], [x + Math.cos(ang) * 8, y + Math.sin(ang) * 8], [x + Math.cos(ang + open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang + open) * 7]], cl ? '#000000' : '#141026');\n      }, { outline: !cl, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n      if (deathT > 0) return;\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const p = pos(w.m), blink = w.blue && fright < 2 && Math.floor(t * 6) % 2, body = w.blue ? (blink ? '#f0f0ff' : '#2a3aff') : w.c;\n        if (w.eyes || cl) r.actor(p.x, p.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n          if (!w.eyes) { px.disc(g, x, y - 1, 4, body); px.rect(g, x - 4, y - 1, 9, 4, body); for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.dot(g, x - 3 + i * 3 + (Math.floor(t * 8) % 2), y + 3, '#000000'); }\n          if (w.blue && !w.eyes) { px.rect(g, x - 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); px.rect(g, x + 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); return; }\n          const [dx, dy] = w.m.dir; px.rect(g, x - 3, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, x - 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff'); px.dot(g, x + 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff');\n        }, { outline: false, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n        else {   // a Blob rig, its colour its own (blue while you can eat it), its eyes on the way it goes\n          const rig = w.rig; rig.C.base = body; rig.C.dk = E.shade(body, -.35); rig.C.lt = E.shade(body, .35);\n          rig.update(1 / 60, { look: w.m.dir, walk: 1, squash: Math.sin(t * 10 + w.i) * .08 });\n          r.actor(p.x, p.y + 3, 0, (g, x, y) => rig.draw(g, x, y, E.VIEWS.threequarter), { outline: true, rim: true, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n          if (w.blue) L.add(p.x, p.y, 6, 22, .5, { color: '#6a7aff' });\n        }\n      }\n      if (readyT > 0) r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, 'READY!', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + (HY + 6) * C8 + 1, '#ffe040', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' }));\n    }\n    function drawInter(r) {\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        const a = inter, y = Y0 + TUN * C8 + 4, x = X0 + a.x;\n        E.font.text(g, 'INTERMISSION', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + 8 * C8, '#ffe070', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' });\n        if (!a.big) { px.disc(g, x, y, 4, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 20, y - 1, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, x - 24, y - 1, 9, 4, '#ff4a4a'); }\n        else { px.disc(g, x + 30, y - 1, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.rect(g, x + 26, y - 1, 9, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.disc(g, x, y, 11, '#ffe040'); px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x - 12, y - 6], [x - 12, y + 6]], '#000000'); }\n      });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'maze', label: 'MAZE', res: [232, 270], about: 'EAT EVERY SEED, DODGE FOUR WISPS', hue: ['#ffe040', '#4ae8ff', '#ff4a8a'], touch: [], extra: [10000], light: .5,\n      begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; over = false; level = 1; inter = null; wisps = wisps || null; build(); reset(); },\n      revive() { over = false; reset(); },   // after a continue: the same maze, everyone back in place\n      force() { over = true; },\n      step, draw, box: () => [X0, Y0 - 12, MW * C8, MH * C8 + 22], edges: () => [X0 - 4, X0 + MW * C8 + 4],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return level; },\n      state: () => ({ hero: [hero.m.cx, hero.m.cy], wisps: wisps.map(w => [w.m.cx, w.m.cy, w.eyes, w.blue]), seeds: seeds.size + power.size, level, fright: +fright.toFixed(3) })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 2. FORMATION =================================== */\n  const FORM = (() => {\n    const FW = 224, FLY = 130;   // the field's width (its height is the screen's: FH), a moth's speed along its path (px/s)\n    let FH = 270;\n    const MOTH = {\n      a: E.sprite(['..y..y..', '.yYyyYy.', 'ybbBBbby', 'bbBwwBbb', '.bBBBBb.', '..b..b..'], { y: '#ffe040', Y: '#fff8a0', b: '#4a8aff', B: '#8ab8ff', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      b: E.sprite(['r......r', '.rRRRRr.', 'rRwRRwRr', '.rRRRRr.', 'r.r..r.r'], { r: '#e03a4a', R: '#ff8a8a', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      boss: E.sprite(['..gGGg..', '.gGwwGg.', 'gGGGGGGg', 'gpGppGpg', '.p.pp.p.', 'p......p'], { g: '#3ad860', G: '#9af0a0', w: '#ffffff', p: '#c050f0' }),\n      hurt: E.sprite(['..pPPp..', '.pPwwPp.', 'pPPPPPPp', 'pgPggPgp', '.g.gg.g.', 'g......g'], { p: '#a050e0', P: '#d8a0ff', w: '#ffffff', g: '#3ad860' })\n    };\n    const SHIP = E.sprite(['...w...', '...w...', '..wrw..', '.wwrww.', 'wwbwbww', 'w.bbb.w', 'r..r..r'], { w: '#f0f0f8', r: '#ff4a4a', b: '#4a8aff' });\n    const ROWS = [['boss', 4], ['b', 8], ['b', 8], ['a', 10], ['a', 10]];\n    const SLOTS = ROWS.flatMap(([kind, n], row) => Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => ({ kind, x: FW / 2 + (i - (n - 1) / 2) * 18, y: 36 + row * 16 })));\n    let cab, demo, foes, shots, bombs, ship, wave, sway, dead, over, readyT, stars = [], X0 = 0, Y0 = 0;\n    // a wave: five groups of eight fly in from alternate sides, a loop on the way, each to its own place (Catmull paths)\n    function newWave() {\n      foes = []; wave++; cab.card('STAGE ' + wave, 1.8); readyT = Math.max(readyT, .6);\n      SLOTS.forEach((s, i) => {\n        const group = Math.floor(i / 8), side = group % 2 ? 1 : -1, k = i % 8;\n        const path = new E.Path([[FW / 2 + side * 150, -20], [FW / 2 + side * 70, 80], [FW / 2 - side * 20, 170], [FW / 2 - side * 70, 120], [FW / 2 - side * 30, 70], [s.x, s.y]], { smooth: 'catmull' });\n        foes.push({ kind: s.kind, hp: s.kind === 'boss' ? 2 : 1, slot: s, path, d: -(group * 1.6 + k * .14) * FLY, state: 'in', x: path.at(0).x, y: -20, a: Math.PI / 2 });\n      });\n    }\n    function begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; wave = 0; over = false; shots = []; bombs = []; sway = 0; dead = 0; readyT = 1.4; ship = { x: FW / 2, y: FH - 28, cool: 0 }; stars = Array.from({ length: 90 }, (_, i) => ({ x: (i * 97) % FW, y: (i * 53) % 600, s: 20 + (i % 3) * 25 })); layout(); newWave(); }\n    // a dive: from its place a swoop out, at the ship (where it is now) and off the bottom; it comes back from the top\n    function dive(f) {\n      const sx = ship.x, out = f.x < FW / 2 ? -1 : 1;\n      f.path = new E.Path([[f.x, f.y], [f.x + out * 30, f.y - 16], [f.x + out * 46, f.y + 20], [sx + (Math.random() - .5) * 50, FH * .62], [sx + out * 40, FH + 24]], { smooth: 'catmull' }); f.d = 0; f.state = 'dive';\n    }\n    const kill = f => { f.hp = 0; cab.add(f.kind === 'boss' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 400 : 150) : f.kind === 'b' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 160 : 80) : (f.state === 'dive' ? 100 : 50), { x: X0 + f.x, y: Y0 + f.y }); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 10); P.bits(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 6, ['#ffe040', '#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a']); A.sfx('explode', { vol: .45 }); };\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      layout(); sway += dt; ship.y = FH - 28;\n      for (const s of stars) s.y = (s.y + s.s * dt) % 600;\n      if (readyT > 0) readyT -= dt;\n      if (dead > 0 && (dead -= dt) <= 0) { const was = cab.p, r = cab.die(); if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; } if (r === 'next') { was.save = { wave, foes }; const s = cab.p.save; if (s) { wave = s.wave; foes = s.foes; for (const f of foes) if (f.state !== 'form') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; } } else { wave = 0; newWave(); } } ship.x = FW / 2; bombs.length = 0; readyT = 1.4; }\n      const live = dead <= 0 && readyT <= 0;\n      if (live) {   // the ship: left and right; two shots on screen at most\n        const mv = demo ? botMove() : I.move()[0]; ship.x = clamp(ship.x + mv * 115 * dt, 10, FW - 10); ship.cool -= dt;\n        if ((demo ? botFire() : I.down('fire')) && ship.cool <= 0 && shots.length < 2) { shots.push({ x: ship.x, y: ship.y - 8 }); ship.cool = .2; A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .35 }); }\n      }\n      for (const s of shots) s.y -= 270 * dt; shots = shots.filter(s => s.y > -10);\n      const sx = Math.sin(sway * 1.2) * 12;\n      let formed = 0;\n      for (const f of foes) {\n        if (f.state === 'in' || f.state === 'dive') {\n          f.d += FLY * (1 + wave * .04) * dt; if (f.d < 0) continue;\n          const p = f.path.at(f.d), u = f.state === 'in' ? Math.min(1, f.d / f.path.length) : 0; f.x = p.x + sx * u * u; f.y = p.y; f.a = p.angle;\n          if (f.d >= f.path.length) { if (f.state === 'dive') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; f.x = f.slot.x + sx; } else f.state = 'form'; }\n          if (f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50 && Math.random() < dt * (.7 + wave * .1)) bombs.push({ x: f.x, y: f.y, vx: (ship.x - f.x) * .35, vy: 125 });\n        } else if (f.state === 'back') { f.y += 90 * dt; f.x += (f.slot.x + sx - f.x) * Math.min(1, dt * 4); f.a = Math.PI / 2; if (f.y >= f.slot.y) f.state = 'form'; }\n        else { f.x = f.slot.x + sx; f.y = f.slot.y + Math.sin(sway * 3 + f.slot.x * .1) * 1.5; f.a = Math.PI / 2; formed++; }\n      }\n      if (live && formed > 3 && Math.random() < dt * (.45 + wave * .15)) { const c = foes.filter(f => f.state === 'form' && f.hp > 0); if (c.length) { const f = c[Math.floor(Math.random() * c.length)]; dive(f); if (f.kind === 'boss') for (const e of c.filter(e => e !== f && e.kind === 'b' && Math.abs(e.slot.x - f.slot.x) < 20).slice(0, 2)) dive(e); A.sfx('whoosh', { vol: .3 }); } }\n      for (const b of bombs) { b.x += b.vx * dt; b.y += b.vy * dt; } bombs = bombs.filter(b => b.y < FH + 10);\n      for (const s of shots) for (const f of foes) if (!s.hit && f.hp > 0 && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(s.x - f.x) < 7 && Math.abs(s.y - f.y) < 6) { s.hit = true; if (--f.hp > 0) { A.sfx('bump'); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 4); } else kill(f); }\n      shots = shots.filter(s => !s.hit); foes = foes.filter(f => f.hp > 0);\n      if (live) for (const o of [...bombs, ...foes]) if (Math.abs(o.x - ship.x) < 6 && Math.abs(o.y - ship.y) < 6) { dead = 1.8; P.explosion(X0 + ship.x, Y0 + ship.y, 4, .9, { sound: true, flash: false, shake: 2, freeze: false }); if (o.hp) kill(o); break; }\n      if (!foes.length && dead <= 0) newWave();\n    }\n    // the demo's pilot: of a step left, none and a step right, the first where no bomb or diving moth will be in the next\n    // half second (a bomb's way read ahead to the ship's row), preferring the way to the moth nearest above; firing when\n    // under one\n    const hitAt = (x, t) => bombs.some(b => { const k = (ship.y - b.y) / b.vy; return k > -.05 && k < t && Math.abs(b.x + b.vx * k - x) < 9; }) || foes.some(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.y - ship.y) < 40 && Math.abs(f.x - x) < 12);\n    const botMove = () => {\n      const t = foes.find(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50) || foes.filter(f => f.d >= 0).reduce((p, f) => !p || Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < Math.abs(p.x - ship.x) ? f : p, null);\n      const want = t ? clamp((t.x - ship.x) / 10, -1, 1) : 0, ways = [want, 0, -1, 1].map(m => Math.round(m)), q = m => clamp(ship.x + m * 115 * .3, 10, FW - 10);\n      for (const m of ways) if (!hitAt(q(m), .8) && !hitAt((ship.x + q(m)) / 2, .4)) return m === Math.round(want) ? want : m;\n      return ship.x < FW / 2 ? 1 : -1;\n    };\n    const botFire = () => foes.some(f => f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < 8);\n    function layout() { FH = Math.max(270, game.H - 4); X0 = Math.round((game.W - FW) / 2); Y0 = Math.round((game.H - FH) / 2); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), x0 = X0, y0 = Y0;\n      if (cl) r.sky(['#000000', '#000000']); else {\n        SPACE[0].draw(r);\n        r.decal(g => {   // a ringed gas giant low in the field, lit from the upper right: the ring's far half, the planet's banded\n          // shading (discs stepped toward the light), the ring's near half\n          const [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), cx = Math.round(ox + x0 + FW * .24), cy = Math.round(oy + y0 + FH - 40), R = 40;\n          const ring = near => { for (let a = 0; a < TAU; a += .012) { if ((Math.sin(a) > 0) !== near) continue; for (const [k, c] of [[1.55, '#8a6aa8'], [1.7, '#c8a8e0'], [1.85, '#6a4a88']]) px.dot(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * R * k, cy + Math.sin(a) * R * k * .22, c); } };\n          ring(false);\n          ['#1a1030', '#2a1a46', '#3e2860', '#563a7a', '#704e94', '#8c66ac', '#a882c2'].forEach((c, k) => px.disc(g, cx + k * 1.4, cy - k * 1.4, R - k * 4.5, c));\n          for (let b = -2; b <= 2; b++) { const y = b * 12 + 3, hw = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, (R - 2) ** 2 - y * y)) - 3; px.blend(g, .16, 'normal', () => px.rect(g, cx - hw + 1, cy + y, hw * 2, 2, b % 2 ? '#2a1640' : '#e8c8a0')); }\n          ring(true);\n        });\n      }\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        for (const s of stars) if (s.y < FH) px.dot(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, s.s > 50 ? '#ffffff' : s.s > 30 ? '#8a8ab0' : '#4a4a6a');\n        for (const s of shots) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .5, 'add', () => px.rect(g, x0 + s.x - 1, y0 + s.y - 1, 3, 7, '#8ad8ff')); px.rect(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 1, 5, '#ffffff'); }\n        for (const b of bombs) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .4, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x0 + b.x, y0 + b.y, 3, '#ff8a4a')); px.rect(g, x0 + b.x - 1, y0 + b.y - 1, 2, 4, '#ff6a4a'); }\n      });\n      // each moth turned to the way it flies (r.sprite's rot; in its place, facing down); the classic turns in 16 steps\n      for (const f of foes) if (f.d >= 0 || f.state !== 'in') r.sprite(x0 + f.x, y0 + f.y, 0, f.kind === 'boss' && f.hp === 1 ? MOTH.hurt : MOTH[f.kind], { rot: f.a + Math.PI / 2, anchor: 'center', steps: cl ? 16 : 32, glow: cl ? 0 : .3 });\n      if (dead <= 0 && !over && (readyT <= 0 || Math.floor(readyT * 8) % 2)) r.sprite(x0 + ship.x, y0 + ship.y, 0, SHIP, { anchor: 'center', glow: cl ? 0 : .4 });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'formation', label: 'FORMATION', res: [232, 270], about: 'MOTHS FLY IN, FORM UP AND DIVE', hue: ['#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a', '#ffe040'], touch: ['fire'], extra: [20000, 70000], light: 0, fills: true,\n      begin, revive() { over = false; ship.x = FW / 2; bombs.length = 0; readyT = 1.4; }, force() { over = true; }, step, draw,\n      box: () => [X0, Y0, FW, FH], edges: () => [X0 - 2, X0 + FW + 2],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return wave; },\n      state: () => ({ ship: +ship.x.toFixed(2), foes: foes.length, wave, shots: shots.length, bombs: bombs.length })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 3. ROCKS =================================== */\n  const ROCKS = (() => {\n    let RW = 320, RH = 240;   // the field: the whole screen (at least 320 x 240), its edges meeting\n    let cab, demo, ship, rocks, shots, saucer, over, wave, deadT, readyT, sparks, X0 = 0, Y0 = 0;\n    // a rock: a ring of lumpy points; size 3 big, 2, 1 small; the smaller, the faster\n    const rock = (x, y, size) => { const n = 8 + size * 2, R = [0, 5, 10, 18][size], a = Math.random() * TAU, sp = (52 - size * 11) * (.6 + Math.random() * .6); return { x, y, vx: Math.cos(a) * sp, vy: Math.sin(a) * sp, size, R, rot: 0, spin: (Math.random() - .5) * 2, pts: Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => { const t = i / n * TAU, k = .75 + Math.random() * .35; return [Math.cos(t) * R * k, Math.sin(t) * R * k]; }) }; };\n    function newWave() { wave++; rocks = []; for (let i = 0; i < 3 + wave; i++) { const edge = Math.random() < .5; rocks.push(rock(edge ? 0 : Math.random() * RW, edge ? Math.random() * RH : 0, 3)); } if (wave > 1) cab.card('WAVE ' + wave, 1.4); }\n    const home = () => Object.assign(ship, { x: RW / 2, y: RH / 2, vx: 0, vy: 0, a: -Math.PI / 2 });\n    function begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; wave = 0; over = false; shots = []; saucer = null; sparks = []; deadT = 0; readyT = 1.2; ship = { cool: 0, thrust: false }; layout(); home(); newWave(); }\n    const wd = (a, b, s) => E.wrapDiff(a, b, s), far = (a, b) => Math.hypot(wd(a.x, b.x, RW), wd(a.y, b.y, RH));\n    const burst = (x, y, n, sp, life, c) => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = Math.random() * TAU, v = sp * (.4 + Math.random() * .6); sparks.push({ x, y, vx: Math.cos(a) * v, vy: Math.sin(a) * v, t: life * (.5 + Math.random() * .5), c }); } };\n    function kill() { deadT = 1.8; A.sfx('boom'); burst(ship.x, ship.y, 24, 80, .9, '#ffe0a0'); game.shake(3); }\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      layout(); if (readyT > 0 && (readyT > .3 || !rocks.some(k => far(k, { x: RW / 2, y: RH / 2 }) < k.R + 40))) readyT -= dt;   // (it comes back once the middle is clear)\n      if (deadT > 0 && (deadT -= dt) <= 0) { const was = cab.p, r = cab.die(); if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; } if (r === 'next') { was.save = { wave, rocks }; const s = cab.p.save; if (s) ({ wave, rocks } = s); else { wave = 0; newWave(); } } home(); readyT = 1.4; shots = shots.filter(s => !s.foe); }\n      const live = deadT <= 0 && readyT <= 0;\n      if (live) {   // turn, thrust (and drift: a little drag), fire, hyperspace (a one-in-ten chance it goes wrong)\n        const turn = demo ? botTurn() : I.move()[0], thr = demo ? botThrust() : I.down('up') || I.down('thrust') || I.move()[1] < -.6;\n        ship.a += turn * 4.4 * dt; ship.thrust = thr;\n        if (thr) { ship.vx += Math.cos(ship.a) * 170 * dt; ship.vy += Math.sin(ship.a) * 170 * dt; if (Math.random() < .6) sparks.push({ x: ship.x - Math.cos(ship.a) * 6, y: ship.y - Math.sin(ship.a) * 6, vx: -Math.cos(ship.a) * 50 + (Math.random() - .5) * 24, vy: -Math.sin(ship.a) * 50 + (Math.random() - .5) * 24, t: .3, c: '#ffb84a' }); }\n        const sp = Math.hypot(ship.vx, ship.vy); if (sp > 220) { ship.vx *= 220 / sp; ship.vy *= 220 / sp; }\n        ship.vx *= Math.exp(-.4 * dt); ship.vy *= Math.exp(-.4 * dt); ship.cool -= dt;\n        if ((demo ? botFire() : I.pressed('fire')) && ship.cool <= 0 && shots.filter(s => !s.foe).length < 5) { shots.push({ x: ship.x + Math.cos(ship.a) * 7, y: ship.y + Math.sin(ship.a) * 7, vx: Math.cos(ship.a) * 290 + ship.vx, vy: Math.sin(ship.a) * 290 + ship.vy, t: .85 }); ship.cool = .12; A.sfx('laser', { vol: .3 }); }\n        if (demo ? botWarp() : I.pressed('warp')) { burst(ship.x, ship.y, 10, 40, .4, '#8ab8ff'); ship.x = Math.random() * RW; ship.y = Math.random() * RH; ship.vx = ship.vy = 0; A.sfx('warp'); if (Math.random() < .1) kill(); }\n      }\n      if (deadT <= 0) { ship.x = E.wrap(ship.x + ship.vx * dt, 0, RW); ship.y = E.wrap(ship.y + ship.vy * dt, 0, RH); }\n      for (const s of shots) { s.x = E.wrap(s.x + s.vx * dt, 0, RW); s.y = E.wrap(s.y + s.vy * dt, 0, RH); s.t -= dt; }\n      for (const k of rocks) { k.x = E.wrap(k.x + k.vx * dt, 0, RW); k.y = E.wrap(k.y + k.vy * dt, 0, RH); k.rot += k.spin * dt; }\n      for (const p of sparks) { p.x += p.vx * dt; p.y += p.vy * dt; p.t -= dt; } sparks = sparks.filter(p => p.t > 0);\n      // the saucer: now and then, across the screen, shooting at you (across the edges: the nearer way)\n      if (!saucer && live && Math.random() < dt * .05 * wave) saucer = { x: 0, y: 30 + Math.random() * (RH - 60), vx: Math.random() < .5 ? 60 : -60, vy: 0, t: 0, cool: 1.2 };\n      if (saucer) {\n        saucer.x = E.wrap(saucer.x + saucer.vx * dt, 0, RW); saucer.t += dt; saucer.vy = Math.sin(saucer.t * 2) * 22; saucer.y = E.wrap(saucer.y + saucer.vy * dt, 0, RH); saucer.cool -= dt;\n        if (saucer.cool <= 0 && live) { const a = Math.atan2(wd(saucer.y, ship.y, RH), wd(saucer.x, ship.x, RW)) + (Math.random() - .5) * .5; shots.push({ x: saucer.x, y: saucer.y, vx: Math.cos(a) * 150, vy: Math.sin(a) * 150, t: 1.4, foe: true }); saucer.cool = 1.4; A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .2, pitch: .6 }); }\n        if (saucer.t > RW / 60) saucer = null;\n      }\n      // hits: your shots split rocks (big 20, middle 50, small 100) and down the saucer (500); rocks, its shots and it on you\n      for (const s of shots) {\n        if (s.t <= 0 || s.foe) continue;\n        for (const k of rocks) if (!k.dead && far(s, k) < k.R) { k.dead = true; s.t = 0; cab.add([0, 100, 50, 20][k.size], { x: X0 + k.x, y: Y0 + k.y }); A.sfx(k.size > 2 ? 'boom' : 'explode', { vol: .4 }); burst(k.x, k.y, 6 + k.size * 3, 60, .6, '#c8d8ff'); if (k.size > 1) for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) rocks.push(rock(k.x, k.y, k.size - 1)); break; }\n        if (s.t > 0 && saucer && far(s, saucer) < 8) { cab.add(500, { x: X0 + saucer.x, y: Y0 + saucer.y }); s.t = 0; burst(saucer.x, saucer.y, 16, 70, .7, '#ff8aa8'); saucer = null; A.sfx('boom'); }\n      }\n      rocks = rocks.filter(k => !k.dead); shots = shots.filter(s => s.t > 0);\n      if (live && (rocks.some(k => far(ship, k) < k.R + 4) || shots.some(s => s.foe && far(s, ship) < 5) || (saucer && far(saucer, ship) < 10))) kill();\n      if (!rocks.length) newWave();\n    }\n    // the demo's pilot: a rock, the saucer or its shot that will pass within reach in the next second and a half is a\n    // threat: turn across its way and thrust out of it (hyperspace when it is a quarter second off); else brake when\n    // drifting, and turn to where the nearest rock will be when a shot gets there (across the edges), firing when facing\n    // it; the saucer first when it is about\n    function threat() {\n      let worst = null, wt = 1.5;\n      const all = [...rocks, ...(saucer ? [Object.assign({ R: 9 }, saucer)] : []), ...shots.filter(s => s.foe).map(s => Object.assign({ R: 3 }, s))];\n      for (const k of all) {\n        const rx = wd(ship.x, k.x, RW), ry = wd(ship.y, k.y, RH), vx = k.vx - ship.vx, vy = k.vy - ship.vy, v2 = vx * vx + vy * vy || 1, t = -(rx * vx + ry * vy) / v2;\n        if (Math.hypot(rx, ry) < k.R + 12) return { k, t: 0, a: Math.atan2(-ry, -rx) };\n        if (t > 0 && t < wt && Math.hypot(rx + vx * t, ry + vy * t) < k.R + 9) { wt = t; worst = { k, t, a: Math.atan2(vy, vx) + (vx * ry - vy * rx > 0 ? -1 : 1) * Math.PI / 2 }; }\n      }\n      return worst;\n    }\n    const brake = () => Math.hypot(ship.vx, ship.vy) > 45 ? Math.atan2(-ship.vy, -ship.vx) : null;\n    function aim() {\n      let b = null, bd = 1e9; for (const k of saucer ? [saucer] : rocks) { const d = far(ship, k); if (d < bd) { bd = d; b = k; } }\n      if (!b) return null; const t = bd / 290; return Math.atan2(wd(ship.y, b.y + b.vy * t, RH), wd(ship.x, b.x + b.vx * t, RW));\n    }\n    const botTurn = () => { const th = threat(), b = brake(), a = th ? th.a : b !== null ? b : aim(); return a === null ? 0 : clamp(E.angDiff(ship.a, a) * 4, -1, 1); };\n    const botFire = () => { const a = aim(); return a !== null && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, a)) < .15; };\n    const botThrust = () => { const th = threat(), b = brake(), a = th ? th.a : b; return a !== null && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, a)) < .6; };\n    const botWarp = () => { const th = threat(); return !!th && th.t < .25 && th.k.R > 3 && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, th.a)) > 1; };\n    function layout() { RW = Math.max(320, game.W); RH = Math.max(240, game.H); X0 = Math.round((game.W - RW) / 2); Y0 = Math.round((game.H - RH) / 2); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), x0 = X0, y0 = Y0;\n      if (cl) r.sky(['#000000', '#000000']); else SPACE[1].draw(r);\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(x0, y0, RW, RH); g.clip();\n        // glowing vector lines: each shape bright over a soft wide glow (classic: plain white lines), at every edge it crosses\n        const vec = (pts, x, y, a, color, closed = true) => {\n          for (const ox of [-RW, 0, RW]) for (const oy of [-RH, 0, RH]) {\n            const Q = pts.map(([u, v]) => [x0 + x + ox + u * Math.cos(a) - v * Math.sin(a), y0 + y + oy + u * Math.sin(a) + v * Math.cos(a)]);\n            if (Q.every(q => q[0] < x0 - 2 || q[0] > x0 + RW + 2) || Q.every(q => q[1] < y0 - 2 || q[1] > y0 + RH + 2)) continue;\n            const n = closed ? Q.length : Q.length - 1;\n            if (!cl) px.blend(g, .3, 'add', () => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) px.line(g, ...Q[i], ...Q[(i + 1) % Q.length], color, 3); });\n            for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) px.line(g, ...Q[i], ...Q[(i + 1) % Q.length], cl ? '#ffffff' : E.shade(color, .45));\n          }\n        };\n        for (const k of rocks) vec(k.pts, k.x, k.y, k.rot, '#8ab8ff');\n        if (deadT <= 0 && (readyT <= 0 || Math.floor(readyT * 8) % 2)) { vec([[8, 0], [-6, -5], [-3, 0], [-6, 5]], ship.x, ship.y, ship.a, '#ffffff'); if (ship.thrust && Math.floor(game.time * 30) % 2) vec([[-4, -2], [-9, 0], [-4, 2]], ship.x, ship.y, ship.a, '#ffb84a', false); }\n        if (saucer) vec([[-9, 0], [-4, -3], [4, -3], [9, 0], [4, 3], [-4, 3], [-9, 0], [9, 0], [4, -3], [2, -6], [-2, -6], [-4, -3]], saucer.x, saucer.y, 0, '#ff6a8a', false);\n        for (const s of shots) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .5, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 2, s.foe ? '#ff6a8a' : '#c8e0ff')); px.rect(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 1, 1, '#ffffff'); }\n        for (const p of sparks) px.dot(g, x0 + p.x, y0 + p.y, cl ? '#ffffff' : p.c);\n        g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n      });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'rocks', label: 'ROCKS', res: [320, 240], about: 'TURN, THRUST, SPLIT THE ROCKS', hue: ['#c8d8ff', '#8ab8ff', '#ff8a4a'], touch: ['fire', 'thrust', 'warp'], every: 10000, light: 0, fills: true,\n      begin, revive() { over = false; home(); readyT = 1.4; }, force() { over = true; }, step, draw,\n      box: () => [X0, Y0, RW, RH], edges: () => [X0 - 2, X0 + RW + 2],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return wave; },\n      state: () => ({ ship: [+ship.x.toFixed(2), +ship.y.toFixed(2)], rocks: rocks.length, wave, shots: shots.length })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 4. THE CABINET: a scene per game, the title, the attract mode =================================== */\n  const GAMES = [MAZE, FORM, ROCKS];\n  const cabs = {}; for (const G of GAMES) cabs[G.id] = new E.Arcade(game, { id: G.id, lives: 3, extra: G.extra || [], every: G.every });\n  const front = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'arcade', idle: 20, demo: 1e9, scores: 6 });   // the title's attract clock (a demo ends itself: endDemo)\n  let pick = 0, players = 1, demoNext = 0, cabsAt = [];\n  function playScene(G) {\n    const cab = cabs[G.id];\n    let demo = false, demoT = 0, stage = 'play', tableT = 0;\n    // the end: each player's initials in turn (the best first) where they make the table, then the table\n    const ending = (order = cab.players.slice().sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score)) => {\n      const p = order.shift(); if (!p) { stage = 'table'; tableT = 0; A.music(null); return; }\n      if (cab.qualifies(p.score)) { stage = 'entry'; if (cab.players.length > 1) cab.say('PLAYER ' + p.n, 30); cab.enter(p.score, '', () => { cab.clear(); ending(order); }); } else ending(order);\n    };\n    const scene = {\n      view: 'overhead', views: ['overhead'], input: KEYS, res: G.res, expand: true, pausable: true, touch: G.touch, camera: { zoom: false },\n      enter(d) {\n        demo = !!(d && d.demo); demoT = 0; stage = 'play'; tableT = 0;\n        game.follow(null); game.cam.bounds = null; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0); game.cam.snap = true;\n        L.enabled = !classic() && G.light > 0; L.ambient = G.light; L.dark = [4, 2, 14]; L.refresh();\n        if (G.id === 'rocks') { game.input.touchSet('thrust', 'THRUST'); game.input.touchSet('warp', 'WARP'); }\n        cab.start(demo ? 1 : players, { demo }); G.begin(cab, demo); A.music(null);\n      },\n      exit() { L.enabled = false; },\n      back() { game.go('arcade'); return true; },\n      update(dt) {\n        const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\n        if (I.pressed('classic')) { game.settings.set('arcadeLook', classic() ? 'remaster' : 'classic'); L.enabled = !classic() && G.light > 0; game.note(classic() ? 'CLASSIC LOOK' : 'REMASTER'); }\n        cab.update(dt);\n        if (demo) { demoT += dt; if (I.anyPressed() || I.clicked() || demoT > 30 || G.over) { front.endDemo(); game.go('arcade', { scores: G.id }, { fade: 'black' }); return; } G.step(dt, I); return; }\n        if (cab.entry || cab.continuing) return;\n        if (stage === 'table') { tableT += dt; if (tableT > 8 || (tableT > 1 && (I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start') || I.clicked()))) game.go('arcade', null, { fade: 'black' }); return; }\n        if (G.over && stage === 'play') { stage = 'cont'; cab.continue(9, yes => { if (yes) { stage = 'play'; G.revive(); } else ending(); }); return; }\n        G.step(dt, I);\n      },\n      draw(r) {\n        G.draw(r); const [e0, e1] = G.edges(), b = G.box(); cabinet(r, e0, e1, G.hue, G.fills ? 0 : b[1], G.fills ? r.H : b[1] + b[3], G.label);\n        if (stage === 'table') { r.overlay(g => { g.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.78)'; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); px.reset(g); }); cab.drawTable(r, '', Math.max(16, Math.round(r.H / 2 - 82)), G.label + ' HIGH SCORES'); }\n        else cab.draw(r, G.box());\n      },\n      /** the end of a game, now, with score (tools/phone-test.mjs: the way to the table): lives to none; the continue when\n       *  cont, else straight to the initials */\n      end(score, cont) { cab.p.score = score; cab.hi = Math.max(cab.hi, score); for (const p of cab.players) p.lives = 0; G.force(); if (!cont) { stage = 'cont'; ending(); } },\n      /** the proof: a scripted game, a hash of where things are and the scores */\n      run: (n = 600) => proof('arcade-' + G.id, n, (i, k) => { walk(i, k, ['left', 'up', 'right', 'down'], 70); if (i % 30 === 5) k.tap('fire'); if (G.id === 'rocks') { if (i % 140 < 40) k.hold('thrust'); else k.up('thrust'); } }, () => [G.state(), cab.players.map(p => [p.score, p.lives])]),\n      state: () => ({ game: G.state(), stage, demo, entry: cab.entry && { name: cab.entry.name.slice(), i: cab.entry.i, score: cab.entry.score }, wheel: cab.entry && cab.wheel, continuing: cab.continuing, scores: cab.players.map(p => p.score), table: cab.table() })\n    };\n    return scene;\n  }\n  for (const G of GAMES) scenes['arcade-' + G.id] = playScene(G);\n  let showTable = null;\n  const go = i => { pick = i; A.sfx('confirm'); game.go('arcade-' + GAMES[i].id, null, { fade: 'black' }); };\n  const title = {\n    view: 'side', views: ['side'], input: KEYS, res: 'ps1', expand: true, pausable: false, touch: [], camera: { zoom: false },\n    enter(d) {\n      game.follow(null); game.cam.bounds = null; game.focus(0, 0, 0); game.cam.snap = true; A.music(SONG); L.enabled = false; game.input.consumeAll();\n      showTable = d && d.scores || null;\n      if (d && d.part && scenes['arcade-' + d.part]) game.go('arcade-' + d.part, null, { fade: 0 });   // #arcade/maze\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      const I = game.input, ph = front.attract(dt);\n      if (ph === 'demo') { const G = GAMES[demoNext++ % GAMES.length]; game.go('arcade-' + G.id, { demo: true }, { fade: 'black' }); return; }\n      if (ph !== 'scores') showTable = null; else if (!showTable) showTable = GAMES[(demoNext + GAMES.length - 1) % GAMES.length].id;\n      if (I.pressed('left')) { pick = (pick + GAMES.length - 1) % GAMES.length; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('right')) { pick = (pick + 1) % GAMES.length; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('up') || I.pressed('down')) { players = 3 - players; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start') || I.pressed('fire')) { go(pick); return; }\n      const tap = I.clicked();\n      if (tap) { const i = cabsAt.findIndex(([x, y, w, h]) => tap[0] >= x && tap[0] < x + w && tap[1] >= y && tap[1] < y + h); if (i >= 0 && i < GAMES.length) go(i); else if (i === GAMES.length) { players = 3 - players; A.sfx('select'); } }\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      r.sky(['#0a0418', '#2a0a3a', '#4a1050']);\n      const t = game.time, [cw, ch] = corner(), top = touch() && r.W / 2 + 120 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) { const x = (i * 71 + t * 6 * (1 + i % 3)) % r.W, y = (i * 37) % (r.H * .7); px.dot(g, x, y, i % 5 ? '#6a5a9a' : '#ffffff'); }\n        px.rect(g, 0, r.H - 30, r.W, 30, '#1a0a26'); for (let x = 0; x < r.W; x += 16) px.rect(g, x + ((x / 16) % 2) * 8, r.H - 30, 8, 1, '#3a1a4a');\n        // the cabinets in a row, as tall as they can stand (to 1.9 times their width), centred on a tall screen\n        const n = GAMES.length, w = Math.min(84, Math.floor((r.W - 24) / n) - 8), gap = 8, x0 = Math.round(r.W / 2 - (n * w + (n - 1) * gap) / 2), hgt = Math.min(Math.round(w * 1.9), r.H - 50 - top - 70), y = Math.max(50 + top, Math.round((r.H - hgt) / 2 - 10));\n        E.font.title(g, 'ARCADE', r.W / 2, y - 40, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffffff', '#ffe040', '#ff8a40', '#ff4a8a'], depth: 3 });\n        cabsAt = [];\n        GAMES.forEach((G, i) => {   // a cabinet: a lit marquee, a screen showing the game's own picture, the control panel\n          const x = x0 + i * (w + gap), on = i === pick, sh = Math.round(hgt * .5);\n          cabsAt.push([x, y, w, hgt]);\n          px.rect(g, x, y, w, hgt, on ? '#3a2a5a' : '#221636'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 1, on ? '#8a6ac0' : '#3a2a50');\n          px.rect(g, x + 2, y + 2, w - 4, 13, G.hue[0]); px.blend(g, .3, 'add', () => px.rect(g, x + 2, y + 2, w - 4, 6, '#ffffff'));\n          E.font.text(g, G.label, x + w / 2, y + 6, '#0a0614', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n          const sx = x + 5, sy = y + 19, sw = w - 10; px.rect(g, sx, sy, sw, sh, '#000000');\n          g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(sx, sy, sw, sh); g.clip();\n          if (i === 0) { for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) px.rect(g, sx + 8 + k * 9, sy + sh / 2, 2, 2, '#ffe9a0'); const hx = sx + 6 + (t * 14) % (sw - 12); px.disc(g, hx, sy + sh / 2 + 1, 4, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, hx - 14, sy + sh / 2, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, sx, sy + 4, sw, 2, '#2a6a32'); px.rect(g, sx, sy + sh - 6, sw, 2, '#2a6a32'); }\n          if (i === 1) { for (let k = 0; k < 8; k++) px.rect(g, sx + 6 + (k % 4) * 14 + Math.sin(t * 1.5) * 4, sy + 8 + Math.floor(k / 4) * 10, 6, 4, k < 4 ? '#3ad860' : '#4a8aff'); px.rect(g, sx + sw / 2 - 2 + Math.sin(t) * 18, sy + sh - 9, 5, 5, '#f0f0f8'); px.rect(g, sx + sw / 2 + Math.sin(t) * 18, sy + sh - 18 - (t * 60) % 30, 1, 4, '#ffffff'); }\n          if (i === 2) { for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) { const cx = sx + 10 + ((k * 23 + t * 9) % (sw - 10)), cy = sy + 10 + ((k * 17 + t * 5) % (sh - 14)), R = 3 + k % 3 * 2; for (let q = 0; q < 6; q++) px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(q) * R, cy + Math.sin(q) * R, cx + Math.cos(q + 1) * R, cy + Math.sin(q + 1) * R, '#c8d8ff'); } const a = t * 1.3, cx = sx + sw / 2, cy = sy + sh / 2; px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * 5, cy + Math.sin(a) * 5, cx + Math.cos(a + 2.5) * 4, cy + Math.sin(a + 2.5) * 4, '#ffffff'); px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * 5, cy + Math.sin(a) * 5, cx + Math.cos(a - 2.5) * 4, cy + Math.sin(a - 2.5) * 4, '#ffffff'); }\n          g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n          px.blend(g, .12, 'add', () => px.rect(g, sx, sy, sw, 3, '#ffffff'));\n          const py = sy + sh + 5; px.rect(g, x + 3, py, w - 6, Math.max(10, hgt - (py - y) - 14), '#140c22');\n          px.disc(g, x + 14, py + 8, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, x + 13, py + 1, 2, 7, '#c8c8d0'); px.disc(g, x + w - 22, py + 8, 3, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x + w - 12, py + 8, 3, '#4ae8ff');\n          const hi = cabs[G.id].table()[0]; E.font.text(g, 'HI ' + (hi ? hi.score : 0), x + w / 2, y + hgt - 10, '#c8b8f0', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n          if (on) { const k = Math.floor(t * 3) % 2 ? '#ffffff' : '#ffe040'; px.rect(g, x - 2, y - 2, w + 4, 2, k); px.rect(g, x - 2, y + hgt, w + 4, 2, k); px.rect(g, x - 2, y, 2, hgt, k); px.rect(g, x + w, y, 2, hgt, k); }\n        });\n        // one or two players (up and down, or a tap on it)\n        const by = y + hgt + 6, bw = 96, bh = touch() ? 34 : 16; cabsAt.push([Math.round(r.W / 2 - bw / 2), by, bw, bh]);   // (a thumb's size on a touch screen)\n        px.rect(g, r.W / 2 - bw / 2, by, bw, bh, '#2a1a3e'); E.font.text(g, players === 1 ? '< 1 PLAYER >' : '< 2 PLAYERS >', r.W / 2, by + bh / 2 - 3, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', outline: false });\n        E.font.text(g, GAMES[pick].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 22, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n        E.font.text(g, touch() ? 'TAP A CABINET TO PLAY' : game.input.lastDevice === 'gamepad' ? 'D-PAD + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   Y CLASSIC LOOK' : 'ARROWS + ENTER   C CLASSIC LOOK', r.W / 2, r.H - 11, '#9a8ac8', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n      });\n      if (showTable) { r.overlay(g => { g.fillStyle = 'rgba(4,2,12,.88)'; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); px.reset(g); }); cabs[showTable].drawTable(r, '', Math.max(16, Math.round(r.H / 2 - 82)), GAMES.find(G => G.id === showTable).label + ' HIGH SCORES'); }\n    },\n    back() { game.go('title'); return true; },\n    /** the bot (tools/kits-test.mjs): each game played by its own demo pilot, from a seed, until it clears two stages (or\n     *  five minutes of game time, or its lives run out); then the attract mode left alone: the demo it starts, the table, the title again. What they reached */\n    bot() {\n      const was = Math.random, out = {}, A0 = game.audio.muted; Math.random = E.rng(9);\n      try {\n        for (const G of GAMES) {\n          game.time = 0; game.go('arcade-' + G.id, { demo: true }, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n          const cab = cabs[G.id]; let t = 0, cleared = 0;\n          while (t < 300 && !G.over && G.level < 3) { cab.update(1 / 120); G.step(1 / 120, game.input); t += 1 / 120; if (G.level > 1 && !cleared) cleared = Math.round(t); }\n          out[G.id] = { score: cab.players[0].score, level: G.level, cleared, lives: cab.players[0].lives, over: !!G.over, seconds: Math.round(t) };\n        }\n        game.go('arcade', null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120); front.wake();\n        game.advance(front.o.idle + .5); const demoAt = game.sceneName;\n        for (let i = 0; i < 40 && game.sceneName !== 'arcade'; i++) game.advance(1);\n        const back = game.sceneName, table = front.phase === 'scores'; game.advance(front.o.scores + .5);\n        out.attract = demoAt.startsWith('arcade-') && back === 'arcade' && table && front.phase === 'title';\n        out.errors = game.errors.length; return out;\n      } finally { Math.random = was; }\n    },\n    /** what the title shows: the game picked, one or two players, where each cabinet is (and the players button, last) on\n     *  screen, the attract mode's phase */\n    state: () => ({ pick, players, cabs: cabsAt, phase: front.phase, table: showTable }),\n    /** the proof: each game's proof, one after the other */\n    run: (n = 600) => GAMES.map(G => scenes['arcade-' + G.id].run(n)).join('-')\n  };\n  return title;\n})();\nscenes.arcade = ARCADE;\n\n/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n// a genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\nfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\ntitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n// #<slice>/<part> jumps in (#arcade/maze, #shooter/horizontal): the slice's enter(data) gets { part }; a part that is a\n// scene of its own (the slice's parts: { battle: 'rpg-battle' }) starts there\nconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: to || (sc ? first : 'title'), data: sc && part ? { part } : undefined });\nwindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu };   // for tests\n})();\n/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
