{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"agent_message","text":"The remote repair test exposed a real collision bug: at an exact bunker-cell boundary, a shot could keep hitting a neighboring cell that erosion never removed. Hits now erode the cell the collision resolver actually selected, and a regression test covers that firing lane. Remote repair, death, and respawn checks pass. Broader input tests also found duplicate click handling; I’m fixing that with wake-event consumption.\n"}}
