{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -l vendor/hub\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('evidence/issues.json')\nissues=[\n {'id':'I01','severity':'major','problem':'Title music initialized Web Audio before a real gesture, producing a browser autoplay warning.','caughtBy':'Export browser no-warning check','fix':'Wait for a trusted gesture and native audio.ready before scheduling music or SFX.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I02','severity':'minor','problem':'Title footer text rows overlapped at 1920x1080.','caughtBy':'Visual inspection of title-1080.png','fix':'Separate hint, cartridge metadata and input prompts; increase main menu text.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I03','severity':'major','problem':'Play-screen early layout return left the contextual repair target and menu rectangles stale.','caughtBy':'Code review of touch layout update path','fix':'Recompute field hit targets and repair availability during every update, independent of draw.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I04','severity':'critical','problem':'A shot aligned to a bunker cell boundary could repeatedly collide with an adjacent cell that erosion did not remove.','caughtBy':'Lossy Hub semantic remote fire/repair test; diagnosed in repairDebug snapshot','fix':'Pass the actual first-hit cell to erosion and crater about that cell; add an ordinary hold-fire regression at x306.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I05','severity':'major','problem':'Pointer-down actions and native compatibility clicks could advance credits twice and reuse an attract wake click.','caughtBy':'Browser credits pagination and consumed click wake checks','fix':'Use one pointer action route, and consume the full wake gesture including a click following wake motion.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I06','severity':'minor','problem':'Pointer capture rejects synthetic touch pointer IDs, interrupting the touch test stand-in.','caughtBy':'Phone/tablet multitouch and cancellation emulation','fix':'Capture real pointers defensively, while allowing synthetic test pointer events to exercise the same action route.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I07','severity':'major','problem':'Desktop-sized menu rows would be too small as touch targets on a portrait phone.','caughtBy':'Portrait scale calculation and follow-up CSS target-size assertions','fix':'Use 56-logical-unit portrait rows, larger type and generous spacing.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I08','severity':'minor','problem':'Native touch START remained visible alongside the custom menu button.','caughtBy':'Portrait screenshot inspection','fix':'Default native touch-button layer to Hidden; keep the relative touch handler and contextual repair.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I09','severity':'minor','problem':'Developer entry directly into flagship core phase displayed the emitter-phase instruction.','caughtBy':'Visual inspection of flagship-core-1080.png','fix':'Choose phase-specific entry and control text.','status':'fixed'},\n {'id':'I10','severity':'minor','problem':'Bright planet bands weakened the contrast of light-colored alien silhouettes.','caughtBy':'Combat screenshot inspection','fix':'Give every original sprite a dark native pixel outline.','status':'fixed'}\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps({'policy':'Count distinct root causes; repeated assertions and harness retries are not additional issues.','issues':issues},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
