.\n\nPhysical gamepad feel, human listening, real TV distance and physical iOS behavior are unknown. Phone/tablet and gamepad tests are emulations. Audio assertions prove finite signals, bounded gains and mute silence, not aesthetic quality.\n\n## Source and provenance\n\nSee \"'`evidence/research.md`, `evidence/issues.json`, `vendor/engine/PATCHES.md`, and `src/report.json`. The last object is the single source for the in-game source/feedback pages and the generated root `exit-interview.json`.\n\nOriginal game code and pixel assets were authored for this task. The full engine remains unchanged under its included MIT license. The pristine AI Hub session client is the first script after the character-set declaration, as required by Protocol v1.\nEOF\ncat > evidence/research.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Research and provenance\n\nThe source brief is interpreted as Bally's 1979 Astrocade Space Invaders, subsequently Astro Battle, rather than Sidam's similarly named arcade game. This is the plan's working interpretation, not a new release-history claim. The renamed manual itself bears a 1981 copyright.\n\nExamined sources:\n\n- [Bally Alley HTML manual](https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/html_manuals/astro_battle.htm), read in full. It establishes horizontal base movement, upward fire, four difficulty settings, damage to bunkers by both sides, accelerating survivors, lower subsequent formations, a harmless bonus parent ship, row-based 10/20/30/40 scores, 100/200/300 parent bonuses, three starting bases, one extra at 1,000 and an ending after six formations.\n- [Five-page manual scan](https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/pdf_manuals/Astro_Battle.pdf), saved as \"'`manual.pdf`. Rasterized and inspected the playing-instructions page, scan page 3. The web screenshot endpoint could not return the scan; local rasterization supplied the visual evidence. Text extraction on these scans is unavailable because the pages are images.\n- [October 1982 comparison article](https://ballyalley.com/articles_and_news/Video_Games_October_1982.pdf), saved as `comparison.pdf`. Inspected scan page 4 / printed page 66. It describes colorful crustacean-like marchers, the unusual marching beat, saucer event and the finite sixth-attack ending. No historical audio listening was performed.\n- [Cartridge-video archive](https://ballyalley.com/astrocade_videos/cartridge_videos/cartridge_videos.html), including its Astro Battle link to [Nice and Games, LSYrGZm0I9Q](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LSYrGZm0I9Q). Metadata identifies a 353-second review published January 29, 2010. Direct MP4 download was denied with HTTP 403. A short HLS clip requested around 80-96 seconds succeeded; see `source-clip.mp4` and `source-filmstrip.png`. Examined eight frames spaced two seconds apart: the cartridge and difficulty menus, horizontal movement of colored four-row troops, alternating silhouettes, a low yellow cannon, four orange arch-shaped bunkers and their visible erosion. The short clip is silent video, so exact historical sound events and audio cadence remain unknown. No ROM or commercial asset extraction was used.\n\nThe game uses original silhouettes and authored four-row/eight-column arrangements; that column count is a new layout, not a claim about the source. Simultaneous/online co-op, deterministic salvage and repair, specialist armour/bombardiers, new locations, the hostile flagship and all writing are original additions. The bonus saucer remains harmless and is visually distinct from the flagship. No fuel/docking loop or diving enemies were imported.\n\nEngine reference: my-3D2dge handoff v0.89.1 at `8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691`. Read README, API card, style/animation/headless guidance, arcade kit lifecycle and native headless example. The arcade helper alternates two-player turns and was not used for simultaneous co-op. Its endpoint bullet helpers were not used for damage.\n\nNetworking reference: AI Hub Protocol v1 / session client 1.4.0 at `35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869`. Read README, complete client and shared-world arena example. Vendor includes the matching official harness, bridge and round coordinator. Complete world snapshots are approximately a few KB, so they use reliable messages at 10 Hz within the 16 KB / 20 sends per second contract. Inputs are bounded 10 Hz unreliable heartbeats with repair-edge acknowledgment and sequence acknowledgment for movement. Remote presentation interpolates immutable positions; damage, masks, score and results are authoritative.\n\nResearch files are evidence only and are not loaded by the exported game.\nEOF\ncat > vendor/engine/PATCHES.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Engine patch record\n\nThe full \"'`my-3d2dge.js` is unchanged from the v0.89.1 handoff at commit `8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691`. No separate included module or agent-edition copy is loaded with it.\n\nGame-level adapters:\n- Adapt the arcade kit'\"'s native Game lifecycle, fixed overhead camera, sprite/animation, palette, audio and settings facilities.\n- Use one serializable, seeded shared battle simulation for simultaneous co-op; do not use the arcade helper's alternating-turn multiplayer.\n- Resolve swept first hits against the actual bunker cell, ship, enemy or flagship part; do not invoke endpoint damage helpers afterward.\n- Supply concise native-pixel controller-first screens, safe gesture audio unlock, contextual touch controls and local Hub overlays using documented opt-outs (\"'`menu:false`, `autoPause:false`, `pausable:false`). Native settings/set/reset, full-screen and input ownership remain in use.\n- Derive authoritative online ticks from AI Hub time, with a complete reliable snapshot strategy. Engine timeScale remains one; standalone developer time is a run-owned simulation accumulator.\n\nThe build escapes literal closing-script sequences only when embedding engine source in HTML. This does not alter the vendored engine file or executing JavaScript semantics.\nEOF\ncat > vendor/hub/PROVENANCE.md <<'\"'EOF'\nAI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0. All protocol assets vendored unchanged from michaelcrosato/ai-hub commit 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Includes README.md, session.js, bridge.js, round.js, harness.html and examples/arena.html. The repository archive supplied no top-level license file. The session client banner is preserved verbatim and the complete client is embedded as the first script immediately following meta charset. No Hub source patches.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/app.js');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace(\\\"btn('SEED & TIME', () => show('time')), btn('RESTART ENCOUNTER'\\\", \\\"btn('SEED & TIME', () => show('time')), btn('STATE SUMMARY', () => show('state')), btn('RESTART ENCOUNTER'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"      case 'seed': return\\\", \\\"      case 'state': return { title: 'DEFENSE DIAGNOSTICS', kicker: 'READ-ONLY STATE SUMMARY', rows: [btn('BACK', back)] };\\\\n      case 'seed': return\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"['controls', 'about', 'records', 'results'].includes(app.screen)\\\", \\\"['controls', 'about', 'records', 'results', 'state'].includes(app.screen)\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"      if (app.screen === 'results') drawResults(g, W, H, s);\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"      if (app.screen === 'results') drawResults(g, W, H, s);\n      if (app.screen === 'state') {\n        const y = H > 400 ? H * .34 : 76, network = app.session;\n        const lines = ['TICK ' + s.tick + ' / EPOCH ' + s.epoch + ' / SEED ' + s.seed,\n          'ENCOUNTER ' + (s.encounter + 1) + ' / ' + s.phase.toUpperCase(),\n          'ENEMIES ' + s.enemies.length + ' / SHOTS ' + s.shots.length + ' / SALVAGE ' + s.pickups.length,\n          'ACTIVE ' + s.ships.filter(p => p.active).length + ' / PENDING ' + s.ships.filter(p => p.wait).length + ' / RESERVE ' + s.reserve,\n          'SCORE ' + s.score + ' / EXTRA ' + (s.extra ? 'AWARDED' : 'AT 1000'),\n          'REPAIRS ' + s.stats.repairs + ' / LOSSES ' + s.stats.deaths,\n          network ? 'NET ' + network.debug.sent + ' SENT / ' + network.debug.received + ' RECEIVED / MAX ' + network.debug.maxBytes + 'B' : 'LOCAL AUTHORITY / RNG ' + s.rng];\n        lines.forEach((line, i) => text(g, line, W / 2 - 190, y + i * (H > 400 ? 27 : 13), i % 2 ? '#9ecdc8' : '#d3ded8', H > 400 ? 2 : 1));\n      }\\\"\\\"\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/view.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"flash: e.hit ? '#fff1d7' : undefined\\\", \\\"flash: e.hit && game.settings.flashes > 0 ? '#fff1d7' : undefined\\\").replace(\\\"flash: p.shield > 0 &&\\\", \\\"flash: game.settings.flashes > 0 && p.shield > 0 &&\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/sim.mjs');s=p.read_text();pos=s.index(\\\"test('Saucer is harmless\\\")\ns=s[:pos]+\\\"\\\"\\\"test('An exposed bombardier telegraphs then releases its broad crater bomb', () => {\n  const q = fresh(); q.startEncounter(3); q.s.phase = 'active'; q.s.fireClock = 1; q.s.enemies = [q.s.enemies.find(e => e.type === 'B')]; run(q, 1.1);\n  assert(q.s.events.some(e => e.type === 'warning' && e.broad)); assert(q.s.shots.some(b => b.kind === 'crater'));\n});\n\\\"\\\"\\\"+s[pos:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/engine.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"'resources', 'time', 'seed'\\\", \\\"'resources', 'time', 'state', 'seed'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('evidence/issues.json');issues=json.loads(p.read_text());last=issues['issues'][-1];last['problem']='Long touch control descriptions overflowed the portrait right edge.';last['caughtBy']='Phone control-card screenshot inspection';last['fix']='Wrap descriptions to the available width and increase row spacing.'\nissues['issues'].append({'id':'I13','severity':'minor','problem':'About page count overlapped the last button, and longer text needed a per-layout page capacity.','caughtBy':'Credits screenshot inspection and per-layout text measurement','fix':'Move page numbering to the header and split long report text into readable pages.','status':'fixed'})\np.write_text(json.dumps(issues,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('src/report.json');x=json.loads(p.read_text())\nx['sourceInformation']['testing']='132 automated checks: deterministic simulation, complete ordinary-action standard solo and co-op campaigns, an ordinary campaign through the native exported scripts, headless draw/UI, Chromium input/audio, standard gamepad stubs, phone/tablet emulation, Firefox/WebKit startup/input smoke, isolated file export, and the pinned Hub harness plus semantic state checks. Hub scenarios use 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss. Physical controller feel, human listening, real TV distance, physical iOS behavior and novice first-run duration are unknown.'\nx['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native E.anim, game.tween and engine fixed clocks; procedural recoil, beat-synchronized march poses, shell breaks, repair clusters, debris and flagship opening/closing states.'\nx['testingFeedback']=[\n '13 distinct issues across automated checks, visual inspection and implementation review; all fixed. The issue log records root causes, severity and the check that caught each one.',\n '1 critical issue: at an exact bunker-cell boundary, repeated shots could hit a neighboring cell that erosion never removed. Swept hits now erode the actual collided cell, with a regression test.',\n 'The lossy Hub semantic fire-and-repair check. It exposed the boundary collision bug even though complete ordinary campaign bots and transport conformance passed; it also verifies remote masks, repair cost, deaths, protected respawns and terminal agreement.',\n 'The initial boot-only smoke check. It confirmed startup and native drawing but could not establish ordinary playability or remote world agreement.'\n]\nx['engineFeedback'][1]='Yes: sampling only held input missed quick mouse repair clicks, and mixing pointer-down actions with native compatibility clicks advanced menus twice. One action route and pressed-edge sampling fixed these. The documented arcade helper alternates players, so simultaneous co-op uses a shared simulation.'\np.write_text(json.dumps(x,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../PROGRESS.md');s=p.read_text();s += '''\\\\n## Verification checkpoint before final report build\\\\n- Quiet full suite is running after final collision, input, portrait layout and network interpolation changes. Expected132 checks (23 simulation,13 native engine,10 session unit,59 browser,27 official/semantic Hub). Final result must be checked, not assumed.\\\\n- Latest separate browser suite:59 checks,0 failures. Covers quick right-click repair, two standard pads including L1 repair and unplug/reclaim, portrait controls/contextual repair/cancel/wake, audio signal and mute, storage blocked/malformed, Firefox/WebKit.\\\\n- Latest Hub suite:27 checks,0 failures. All official one/two seat/host-leave/server cases pass. Semantic repair/death/respawn/overlay and terminal outcome agree across copies; terminal host/guest tick572 both TIME EXPIRED.\\\\n- Final normal simulation evidence after cell fix: solo310.62s,6780 points,1death,42 repairs; co-op219.83s,7480 points,1death,47 repairs. Bots use ordinary actions and full damage/resources. These are skilled automatic runs, not human novice timing.\\\\n- State summary, two-phase developer selection, pad seed digit entry, immediate numeric tuning and reliable complete world snapshots with movement/repair acknowledgments are implemented. Remote positional interpolation is draw-only.\\\\n-13 distinct issues recorded in evidence/issues.json;1critical (cell-boundary erosion). All listed fixes implemented. Report src/report.json finalized around that evidence but must rebuild and verify exact artifact.\\\\n- README.md, evidence/research.md, vendor/engine/PATCHES.md and vendor/hub/PROVENANCE.md written. Engine and Hub remain unmodified.\\\\n- Remaining: inspect latest emitter/core and repaired phone/control/credit captures; await full suite; build finalized report, rerun final artifact checks; write evidence verification summary and final progress completion.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
