{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_119","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('..');report=json.loads(Path('src/report.json').read_text());exit_report=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text());assert report==exit_report\nverify=json.loads(Path('evidence/verification.json').read_text());artifact=root/verify['artifact'];assert hashlib.sha256(artifact.read_bytes()).hexdigest()==verify['artifactSHA256'];assert verify['checks']==133 and verify['failures']==0\nassert Path('index.html').read_bytes()==artifact.read_bytes()\nissues=json.loads(Path('evidence/issues.json').read_text())['issues'];assert len(issues)==15 and sum(i['severity']=='critical' for i in issues)==1 and all(i['status']=='fixed' for i in issues)\nsim=json.loads(Path('evidence/sim-tests.json').read_text());native=json.loads(Path('evidence/engine-tests.json').read_text());browser=json.loads(Path('evidence/browser-tests.json').read_text());hub=json.loads(Path('evidence/hub-tests.json').read_text())\nlines=['# Final verification','',f\\\"Artifact: \"'`{verify['\"'artifact']}\"'`\",f\"SHA-256: `{verify['\"'artifactSHA256']}\"'`\",f\"Bytes: {artifact.stat().st_size}\",'\"'',f\\\"Command: \"'`node tools/test.mjs` — {verify['\"'checks']} checks, {verify['failures']} failures.\\\",'']\nfor suite in verify['suites']:lines.append(f\\\"- {suite['suite']}: {suite['count']} checks, {suite['failed']} failures\\\")\nlines += ['', '## Ordinary-rules completion evidence','', 'These pilots observe state and submit ordinary movement, fire and repair. They do not modify health, resources, tuning, encounters or invulnerability. All runs use standard difficulty.']\nfor c in sim['campaigns']:lines.append(f\\\"- Fixed-step {c['seats']}-seat seed {c['seed']}: victory, {c['seconds']:.2f} simulation seconds, {c['score']} points, {c['stats']['deaths']} deaths, {c['stats']['repairs']} repairs, all six formations and both flagship phases.\\\")\nfor c in native['evidence']:\n if 'nativeCampaignSeconds' in c:lines.append(f\\\"- Native exported solo campaign: victory in {c['nativeCampaignSeconds']:.2f} simulation seconds, {c['score']} points; all eight encounter/phase identities observed.\\\")\n if 'nativeCoopSeconds' in c:lines.append(f\\\"- Native local co-op campaign: victory in {c['nativeCoopSeconds']:.2f} simulation seconds, {c['score']} points; contributions {c['contributions']}; {c['deaths']} deaths. This bot run did not need repairs; explicit pad, touch and remote repair tests cover that action separately.\\\")\nlines += ['', 'These are skilled automatic replays. A novice human first-success duration is unknown; the intended 8–12 minute pacing has not been measured with a human.', '', '## Export, input and sessions','', '- Actual root artifact copied into an isolated evidence directory and opened by file URL. Boot, menus, ordinary play, replay, credits and assets work without development files.', '- Native headless draw and update paths have no errors. Chromium full tests and Firefox/WebKit startup/input smoke pass.', '- Standard-mapping gamepad stubs cover simultaneous play, repair, held confirmation, unplug/reclaim and glyph choice. Phone/tablet profiles cover taps, relative steering, second-contact fire, contextual repair, cancellation, attract wake and credits rotation.', '- Official pinned Hub harness passes supported one-seat and two-seat rounds, host-leave and server-only hosting with latency150ms, jitter50ms and loss5%. All complete flags and pass results are checked.', '- Additional Hub semantics check remote erosion/repair masks and costs, death/reserve/respawn agreement, local overlays, disabled mutations, and a shared terminal TIME EXPIRED outcome before end.', '- Packet strategy: complete reliable snapshots at10Hz, bounded unreliable action heartbeats at10Hz. Repair edges and input sequences are acknowledged. Remote positional interpolation changes no authoritative state.', '', '## Audio and limitations','', f\\\"- Production native synth signal metrics: {json.dumps(browser['observations']['audio'])}\\\", '- Music initializes and resets to0.10. Audio unlock requires a real browser gesture. Muted bus renders zero signal; generated samples are finite and bounded; owned gibberish voices terminate.', '- Physical controller feel, human listening, real TV distance and physical iOS behavior remain unknown. Emulation and signal checks are not claims about those experiences.', '', '## Review and provenance','', '- Fifteen distinct issues were found and fixed; one classified critical. See issues.json for root causes and checks.', '- Visually inspected title/combat hierarchy, native silhouettes, emitter/core distinction and telegraph, TV focus/sliders, portrait controls/occlusion and credits pagination. Final layout regressions also verify the actual page reached.', '- Source research and limits are in research.md. Native engine and pristine Hub client are unchanged and their embedding/integrity is checked.', '- Root exit-interview.json parses, matches src/report.json exactly, and supplies every required source and feedback field. Its same data is embedded in About/Credits. Usage is exactly added on import.', '']\nPath('evidence/verification.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines))\nfolder=Path.cwd().name\nprogress=f'''# PROGRESS.md — Astro Battle Jam\n\nStatus: **COMPLETE**. The final artifact and exact exit interview are built and verified. No required work remains.\n\n## Deliverables\n- \"'`{folder}.html` in the workspace root: complete self-contained game, {artifact.stat().st_size} bytes.\n- `exit-interview.json` beside it: exact TASK.md schema, parsed and matched to the game'\"'s embedded report.\n- \"'`{folder}/`: all development sources, dependencies, research, tests and evidence.\n\nTitle selected with a real random-number generator from 50 original candidates. Implemented PLAN.md using TASK.md and the game-toolchain skill; no subagents used.\n\n## Final verification\n- Command from the development folder: `node tools/test.mjs` (also `npm test`).\n- **133 checks, 0 failures**: simulation23, native engine14, session10, browser59, Hub27.\n- Artifact SHA-256: `{verify['\"'artifactSHA256']}\"'`.\n- Root HTML equals development index.html. Isolated file export, HTTP Hub origin, interview schema and pristine client placement/integrity pass.\n- Detailed evidence: `evidence/verification.json`, `verification.md` and each suite'\"'s \"'`*-tests.json`.\n\n## Completed acceptance checklist\n- [x] Pinned full native engine v0.89.1 and pristine Hub client1.4.0 embedded, no runtime downloads.\n- [x] Seeded120Hz serializable combat, living formation bounds/descent/acceleration, swept first hits, two-missile cap.\n- [x] Four cell-mask bunkers, both-side erosion, deterministic salvage and bounded corridor-preserving repair, full-footprint rebuild.\n- [x] Shared deployments, protected respawn, one-time extra at1000, stable contribution scores and defeat causes.\n- [x] Six authored formations, three locations, ordinary/armoured/bombardier enemies, harmless bonus saucer and original two-phase flagship.\n- [x] Complete normal standard solo/co-op campaigns in pure simulation AND through the native exported game; no cheats.\n- [x] Simultaneous local co-op, two standard pad stubs, keyboard/mouse routing and reconnect seat ownership.\n- [x] Hub host/guest/server authority, reliable complete snapshots, bounded heartbeats/acks, stale input, shared clock, local overlays, departures, time-up and terminal agreement.\n- [x] Title/lobby/controls/settings/pause/dev/records/results; readable paged About/Credits with every source and feedback answer.\n- [x] Ten-second looping isolated attract, consumed wake events, all input families and clean next-run state.\n- [x] Live tuning, seeds, encounter/phase choice, spawns, resources, invulnerability, diagnostics and step/time controls; assisted records separated; Hub mutations disabled.\n- [x] Procedural art/animation/audio, music default/reset10%, trusted gesture unlock, finite signal/mute/voice cleanup checks.\n- [x] Phone/tablet target sizing, contextual repair/cancellation/rotation, blocked/malformed storage, Firefox/WebKit smoke.\n- [x] Final reports, provenance, issue log, licenses, inspected visual evidence and owned server/browser cleanup.\n\n## Results and honest limits\n- Pure simulation standard seed2037: solo310.62s,6780points,1death,42repairs; co-op219.83s,7480points,1death,47repairs.\n- Native exported standard runs: solo259.32s,6880points; local co-op182.76s,6980points, contributions4130/2850. These are skilled bots; novice human first-run duration is unknown.\n-15 distinct recorded issues fixed;1critical: cell-boundary hits could fail to erode the actual collided bunker cell. A hold-fire regression covers it.\n- Physical controller feel, human listening, real TV distance and physical iOS behavior are unknown. All device evidence is emulated.\n\n## Source map\n- `src/content.js`: formations, palettes, four presets and validated tuning bounds.\n- `src/sim.js`: all authoritative rules and serializable world.\n- `src/session.js`: real Hub adapter, snapshots and interpolation.\n- `src/assets.js`, `view.js`, `audio.js`: native pixel assets, presentation and runtime synthesis.\n- `src/app.js`: native engine lifecycle, all screens, inputs, attract and developer tools.\n- `src/report.json`: one source for in-game reports and root exit-interview.json.\n- `tools/build.mjs`: reproducible one-file export. `tools/test.mjs`: quiet verification entry point.\n- `README.md`, `evidence/research.md`, `vendor/engine/PATCHES.md`, `vendor/hub/PROVENANCE.md`: operation and provenance.\n\nRebuild with `npm run build` after source/report changes and run the checks that those changes cover. Current package needs no further edits.\n'\"'''\n(root/'PROGRESS.md').write_text(progress)\nprint(json.dumps({'artifact':str(artifact),'bytes':artifact.stat().st_size,'checks':verify['checks'],'failures':verify['failures'],'interview':'valid and identical to embedded source report','issues':len(issues),'sha256':verify['artifactSHA256']}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
